<Layout title="About — Zeqing Wang" description="About Zeqing Wang's research interests and approach to research engineering.">
  <article class="about-shell">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I am an M.S. student in Computer Science (Artificial Intelligence) at the University of Southern California. I received my bachelor's degree in Electronic and Computer Engineering from Shanghai Jiao Tong University.</p>
    <p>My research brings together robot learning, world models, uncertainty quantification, 3D vision, and human–robot interaction. I am especially interested in integrated embodied agents that can perceive, reason, remember, act, and collaborate in the physical world.</p>

    <h2>Research interests</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Perception:</strong> multimodal sensing, 3D vision and reconstruction, and grounded world models</li>
      <li><strong>Cognition:</strong> foundation-model reasoning, uncertainty quantification, planning, and persistent memory</li>
      <li><strong>Action:</strong> robot learning, vision-language-action policies, and adaptive control</li>
      <li><strong>Interaction:</strong> human–robot interaction and multi-agent coordination</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>My experience includes robotic world-model evaluation, 3D Gaussian Splatting for VR and haptics, non-rigid 3D reconstruction for robotic surgery, and reinforcement-learning-based human–robot motion planning.</p>
    <p>I work primarily with Python, C++, PyTorch, TensorFlow, OpenCV, Unity, ML-Agents, and Linux.</p>
